1
00:00:06,677 --> 00:00:11,546
-==www.RagBear.com==-
是, 首相  第2季第1集

2
00:00:13,803 --> 00:00:18,747
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:31,970
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=-
翻译: vivitata
校对&时间轴: tpring

4
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:38,929
<font color="#4096d1">落水之人

5
00:00:38,975 --> 00:00:41,901
艾伦 问题是这计划真的不错
Alan, it's really a very reasonable plan.

6
00:00:41,901 --> 00:00:44,917
好 去跟国防部人事主管说啊
Tell that to the Chief of Defence Staff.

7
00:00:45,135 --> 00:00:46,614
他怎么迟到了?不像部队作风
Why is he late? Not very soldierly.

8
00:00:46,614 --> 00:00:49,905
就因为这计划 国防部乱成一团了
It's this plan. The Ministry's in turmoil.

9
00:00:49,905 --> 00:00:53,446
艾伦 不过是军队调动而已 又不是俄国入侵
It's a relocation proposal, not a Russian invasion.

10
00:00:53,615 --> 00:00:58,006
要是倒好了 我们有措施击退他们
Be all right if it was. We know what we could do to repel that.

11
00:00:58,175 --> 00:01:00,973
真能击退吗?      不能
Could you repel it? No.

12
00:01:01,135 --> 00:01:03,422
但不用真的费脑筋嘛
But we don't have to do any thinking about it.

13
00:01:04,349 --> 00:01:06,713
我们站在首相立场上来看
Let's look at this from the PM's point of view.

14
00:01:06,713 --> 00:01:10,087
我们有42万现役军人
We have 420,000 service personnel.

15
00:01:10,255 --> 00:01:11,833
只有2万驻扎在北部
Only 20,000 are stationed in the north.

16
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:14,698
大家几乎都在南部
Almost everything's in the south.

17
00:01:14,698 --> 00:01:17,924
海军在朴茨茅斯 空军在贝德福德
Navy at Portsmouth, Air Force in Bedford

18
00:01:17,924 --> 00:01:19,140
陆军在阿尔德肖特
and the Army in Aldershot.

19
00:01:19,575 --> 00:01:23,329
基本没人在沃什湾以北 高失业率地区
Almost nothing north of The Wash where the unemployment is.

20
00:01:23,495 --> 00:01:26,771
很多军人来自北方      对 可他们在南方消费
Servicemen come from the north. But spend in the south.

21
00:01:26,935 --> 00:01:27,583
没办法      怎么?
Inevitable.

22
00:01:27,583 --> 00:01:29,485
他们人在那里嘛
That's where they are now.

23
00:01:29,895 --> 00:01:34,127
况且 北方也没有可消费的 对吧?
Anyway, there's nothing to spend it on in the north, is there?

24
00:01:34,295 --> 00:01:37,492
国防部人事主管来了      汉弗莱 这做不到...
Chief of Defence Staff. This cannot happen...

25
00:01:37,655 --> 00:01:41,614
别跟我说 我支持你 可这计划太合理了
Don't attack me, I'm on your side, but it is a strong argument.

26
00:01:41,775 --> 00:01:45,094
调20至30万军人去北方
Move 200,000 service personnel up north

27
00:01:45,094 --> 00:01:47,116
能创造无数就业机会
and you create masses of civilian jobs.

28
00:01:47,975 --> 00:01:50,773
勤杂人员 补给 建筑 车船修配
Clerks, suppliers, builders, vehicle maintenance.

29
00:01:50,935 --> 00:01:53,972
3万份军饷花在商店里
300,000 extra pay packets spent in the shops.

30
00:01:54,135 --> 00:01:56,808
几千人你不能说调就调啊
You can't move thousands of men like that.

31
00:01:56,975 --> 00:02:01,003
军队不就这样吗      那还能调回来
I thought that's what you did with armies. You bring 'em back!

32
00:02:01,003 --> 00:02:02,490
这一去就回不来了
This'd be permanent.

33
00:02:02,615 --> 00:02:06,733
盖伊 有军人可以永久驻扎在北方吗?
Guy, can any servicemen be stationed permanently in the north?

34
00:02:06,895 --> 00:02:09,614
低阶的大概可以 下级军官
I suppose other ranks, junior officers,

35
00:02:09,775 --> 00:02:11,197
可你不能让高级军官
but you can't ask senior officers

36
00:02:11,197 --> 00:02:12,955
一辈子住在北方
to live permanently in the north!

37
00:02:14,535 --> 00:02:16,210
他们的夫人受不了
The wives wouldn't stand for it for one thing.

38
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:17,682
子女上学也是难题
Children's schools.

39
00:02:18,175 --> 00:02:21,326
据我所知 北方也有学校吧
I understand there are schools in the north of England.

40
00:02:21,495 --> 00:02:23,748
对 那哈罗德(伦敦豪华商场)呢? 温布尔登呢?
What about Harrods? What about Wimbledon?

41
00:02:23,748 --> 00:02:27,063
赛马 赛艇 陆军海军俱乐部呢?
Ascot? Henley? The Army and Navy Club?

42
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:31,407
我指的是整个文明 北方都没有
I mean civilisation, generally! It's just not on!

43
00:02:31,575 --> 00:02:34,043
盖伊 内阁今天下午就要讨论了
This is being discussed in Cabinet.

44
00:02:34,215 --> 00:02:36,087
得拿出严肃理由
We need more serious arguments

45
00:02:36,087 --> 00:02:38,851
光说军官夫人远离豪华商场可不行
than senior officers' wives being 300 miles from Harrods.

46
00:02:39,575 --> 00:02:43,329
还不够严重? 你我都可能要调过去了
What's more serious?! Chaps like us might have to move up there!

47
00:02:43,495 --> 00:02:46,692
就没有战略上的反对理由吗?
But are there any strategic arguments against the move?

48
00:02:46,855 --> 00:02:48,995
战略能扯出任何理由
We can find those against anything.

49
00:02:48,995 --> 00:02:52,090
经得起民间专家的论证吗?
But would they stand up to expert scrutiny?

50
00:02:52,090 --> 00:02:54,175
不会让民间专家论证的
They won't get expert scrutiny.

51
00:02:54,175 --> 00:02:57,437
我们会列为机密 国防部惯例
We'll make it top secret like we always do with defence.

52
00:02:57,437 --> 00:02:58,285
只给首相过目
Prime Minister only.

53
00:02:58,285 --> 00:03:01,199
那绝对没有专家论证了
Then they certainly won't get expert scrutiny.

54
00:03:02,655 --> 00:03:05,217
可我在想
But I wonder whether we might not do

55
00:03:05,217 --> 00:03:07,746
我们能不能踢人而不踢球
better to play the man instead of the ball.

56
00:03:07,746 --> 00:03:10,609
哪个人?      就业部长
Which man? The Employment Secretary.

57
00:03:10,775 --> 00:03:14,165
计划总归是他提的      没错
This was his suggestion. Ah, yes.

58
00:03:14,335 --> 00:03:15,392
向首相暗示
Suggest to the PM

59
00:03:15,392 --> 00:03:17,788
就业部长阴谋反对他
the Employment Secretary is plotting against him.

60
00:03:18,175 --> 00:03:20,643
有吗?      没有 我没听说
Is he? Not as far as I know.

61
00:03:20,815 --> 00:03:23,098
可问题在于
But the question is whether

62
00:03:23,098 --> 00:03:25,849
能否让首相相信他有
the Prime Minister can be made to believe that he is.

63
00:03:26,135 --> 00:03:28,171
有机会除掉他吗?
Any chance of getting rid of him?

64
00:03:28,335 --> 00:03:32,613
首相? 他刚被驯化啊      不 就业大臣
The PM? He's only just house-trained. The Employment Secretary.

65
00:03:32,775 --> 00:03:34,970
霍华德上将 你难道是说
Field Marshal, are you suggesting

66
00:03:35,135 --> 00:03:37,895
卑微的公务员有权擅自撤换
humble civil servants should presume to remove

67
00:03:37,895 --> 00:03:39,715
女皇政府的内阁大臣?
a member of HM Government from Cabinet?

68
00:03:39,715 --> 00:03:42,933
对      不可能
Yes. Out of the question.

69
00:03:43,095 --> 00:03:46,087
只有首相能撤换大臣
Only the Prime Minister can remove ministers,

70
00:03:46,255 --> 00:03:48,076
可如果首相怀疑
but if the Prime Minister came to suspect

71
00:03:48,076 --> 00:03:50,956
一个内阁成员的忠诚...
the loyalty of a member of his Cabinet

72
00:03:51,455 --> 00:03:53,650
只有重度妄想狂
Only someone with paranoia

73
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:56,357
才会怀疑就业大臣搞阴谋
would suspect the Employment Secretary of a plot.

74
00:03:56,895 --> 00:03:59,887
真的? 那我们有希望了
Really? Then we're in with a chance.

75
00:04:02,215 --> 00:04:04,790
好 其它事宜 就业大臣
Other business. Employment Secretary,

76
00:04:04,790 --> 00:04:06,403
你提请审阅你的报告
you wanted views on your paper.

77
00:04:06,815 --> 00:04:10,524
对 首相 我的计划旨在降低东北部失业率
Yes, my plan to reduce unemployment in the northeast

78
00:04:10,695 --> 00:04:14,165
通过将某些国防机构搬迁过去
by moving various defence establishments up there.

79
00:04:14,335 --> 00:04:16,530
国防部长 你意下如何?
Defence Secretary, what's your view?

80
00:04:16,695 --> 00:04:18,686
我知道 一眼望去
I know, on the face of it,

81
00:04:18,855 --> 00:04:20,599
这一计划貌似减轻了
this plan looks as though it benefits

82
00:04:20,599 --> 00:04:22,523
贫困地区就业压力
employment in depressed areas,

83
00:04:23,055 --> 00:04:25,962
但据我理解 靠的是
but this is to be achieved, as I understand it,

84
00:04:25,962 --> 00:04:28,495
重新部署大多数国防机构
by relocating most defence establishments.

85
00:04:28,815 --> 00:04:32,933
与国防部的干系 和与就业部一样大
This affects the Defence Department as well as Employment.

86
00:04:33,095 --> 00:04:35,806
我需要时间做可行性研究
I need time to do a feasibility study.

87
00:04:36,799 --> 00:04:38,649
还有人有意见吗? 快提
Anybody else have an opinion? Quickly.

88
00:04:38,649 --> 00:04:40,488
首相 我不太了解
I don't know much about it,

89
00:04:40,488 --> 00:04:43,334
不过听起来像是剧变
but it does sound a serious upheaval.

90
00:04:43,375 --> 00:04:45,366
耗资巨大      影响深远
Expensive.         A big move.

91
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:47,526
我支持这项提案
I'm in favour of the proposal.

92
00:04:47,695 --> 00:04:50,926
我也是      绝对的
So am I. Absolutely!

93
00:04:51,095 --> 00:04:54,849
看起来国防大臣要孤军奋战了
Looks as though the Defence Secretary is in a minority of one.

94
00:04:55,015 --> 00:04:57,801
不过首相 我是国防负责人
I am the responsible minister.

95
00:04:57,801 --> 00:05:00,092
这是领土防卫问题
The defence of the realm is in question.

96
00:05:00,092 --> 00:05:03,724
很好 我们周五的会议上再深入讨论
We'll have a full discussion at our next meeting on Friday

97
00:05:03,895 --> 00:05:06,112
然后提交内阁表决
and then put it to Cabinet for approval.

98
00:05:06,112 --> 00:05:08,207
太好了 谢谢 首相
Thank you.

99
00:05:08,207 --> 00:05:10,654
我能否要求会议纪要里记上
May I request that it be noted in the minutes

100
00:05:10,654 --> 00:05:12,982
内阁委员会支持我的提案
that the Cabinet Committee was in favour of my plan

101
00:05:12,982 --> 00:05:15,638
仅有一人反对?
save for one member?

102
00:05:15,615 --> 00:05:19,608
是被重组部门的负责人 这问题可大了
The member whose department would be reorganised. It's a problem.

103
00:05:19,775 --> 00:05:21,699
能否提请国防大臣注意
May I remind the Secretary of State for Defence

104
00:05:21,699 --> 00:05:24,805
举凡问题 都伴随着机遇?
that every problem is also an opportunity?

105
00:05:25,175 --> 00:05:27,530
好啊 好啊
Hear hear!

106
00:05:27,695 --> 00:05:28,974
国防大臣担心
The Secretary fears that

107
00:05:28,974 --> 00:05:31,574
这可能造成某些不期之遇
this may create some insoluble opportunities.

108
00:05:34,055 --> 00:05:36,011
胡说 没那事
Nonsense.

109
00:05:44,495 --> 00:05:48,454
首相      还在啊 汉弗莱?
Er, Prime Minister... Oh, still here, Humphrey?

110
00:05:50,605 --> 00:05:52,175
对 不知能否跟您谈谈
Yes. I wonder if I could have a word about

111
00:05:52,175 --> 00:05:54,023
就业大臣的提案
the Employment Secretary's plan.

112
00:05:55,095 --> 00:05:55,808
行 提案不错吧?
Yes, terrific, isn't it?

113
00:05:55,808 --> 00:05:58,724
国防部人事主管不大喜欢
The service chiefs aren't entirely happy.

114
00:06:00,095 --> 00:06:01,813
好呀
Good.

115
00:06:03,095 --> 00:06:06,690
首相 您在认真听我说吗?      当然
Do I have your full attention? Of course you do.

116
00:06:06,855 --> 00:06:09,449
我顺便看看会议纪要
I'm just reading these notes.

117
00:06:09,615 --> 00:06:13,005
首相 黑斯米尔发生大地震了
Prime Minister, there's been an earthquake in Haslemere.

118
00:06:16,535 --> 00:06:18,093
好呀
Good.

119
00:06:19,935 --> 00:06:22,733
什么?      人事主管不喜欢这个计划
What? The service chiefs don't like this plan.

120
00:06:22,895 --> 00:06:26,258
当然 夫人们去不成网球赛和商场了嘛
Taking their wives away from Wimbledon and Harrods!

121
00:06:26,258 --> 00:06:29,193
首相 您怎能这么说
Prime Minister, that is unworthy.

122
00:06:29,193 --> 00:06:31,541
这和他们的私心毫无关系
Their personal feelings don't come into it.

123
00:06:32,695 --> 00:06:34,885
反对纯粹出于战略考虑
Their objections are entirely strategic.

124
00:06:34,885 --> 00:06:36,322
战略 可不是嘛
Oh, strategic, of course.

125
00:06:37,175 --> 00:06:38,993
海军部需要深海港
Admiralty needs a deep-water port

126
00:06:38,993 --> 00:06:41,637
所以要设在巴思 离海30里
so that has to be at Bath 30 miles inland.

127
00:06:42,935 --> 00:06:45,362
水兵是保卫挪威(英国以北)的
The job of the Marines is to defend Norway,

128
00:06:45,362 --> 00:06:47,440
所以驻扎在普利茅斯(英国西南)
so we station them at Plymouth.

129
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,808
陆军车辆在苏格兰检测
Army vehicle trials take place in Scotland,

130
00:06:49,808 --> 00:06:53,274
所以军工部当然得在萨里(英国东南)
so the engineering establishment has to be in Surrey.

131
00:06:53,309 --> 00:06:56,486
这些都是特例
Well, these are just isolated examples.

132
00:06:58,175 --> 00:07:01,884
我还有700个"特例"呢
I've got another 700 isolated examples.

133
00:07:02,055 --> 00:07:03,864
你为什么反对它 汉弗莱?      我 首相?
Why are you against it, Humphrey?

134
00:07:03,864 --> 00:07:05,883
我保证我绝无反对
I assure you I'm not against it.

135
00:07:05,935 --> 00:07:07,936
我只是为您提出合理的问题
I'm simply furnishing you with the appropriate questions

136
00:07:07,936 --> 00:07:09,639
比如成本
like that of cost.

137
00:07:09,639 --> 00:07:12,729
这就是妙处 它能挣钱
That's the beauty of it it makes money.

138
00:07:12,895 --> 00:07:14,945
把南方那些贵重机构卖了
We sell all these expensive properties in the south

139
00:07:14,945 --> 00:07:16,740
一路北上
and move "up north"!

140
00:07:18,335 --> 00:07:21,133
您觉得就业部长干得好吗?
You think the Employment Secretary has done well?

141
00:07:21,295 --> 00:07:25,083
是啊 他这人不错      我完全同意 首相
Indeed I do. He's a good chap. Oh, I quite agree.

142
00:07:25,255 --> 00:07:28,611
简直才华横溢
Absolutely brilliant.

143
00:07:28,775 --> 00:07:30,766
智慧超群
Superb intellect.

144
00:07:30,935 --> 00:07:34,312
步伐稳健 手腕出众 形象高大
Strong footwork, excellent elbows. A major figure,

145
00:07:34,312 --> 00:07:35,186
毫无疑问
without a doubt.

146
00:07:35,695 --> 00:07:39,847
也没那么好吧      但他这人不错 您说是吧?
He's not that good. But he is a good chap, wouldn't you say?

147
00:07:40,015 --> 00:07:43,564
是啊 我刚说过      对 当然 很得人心
I've just said so. Oh, yes, indeed. Very popular.

148
00:07:43,735 --> 00:07:46,295
是吗?      可不是嘛
Is he? Oh, yes!

149
00:07:46,455 --> 00:07:48,844
也没那么得人心吧?      当然了
Not as popular as that, surely? Oh, yes.

150
00:07:49,015 --> 00:07:53,327
在白厅和议会各党 左右逢源      恐怕是的
In Whitehall and with the parliamentary party. I suppose, yes.

151
00:07:53,495 --> 00:07:56,373
据说和草根阶级也是      有吗?
And with the grass roots, I'm told. Are you?

152
00:07:56,535 --> 00:08:00,210
在内阁也一呼百应 对吧      是吗?
And he has quite a following in Cabinet, too. Does he?

153
00:08:00,375 --> 00:08:02,611
实际上 已经有人在说
People are beginning to talk about him

154
00:08:02,611 --> 00:08:04,354
让他接任首相了
as the next Prime Minister.

155
00:08:04,415 --> 00:08:09,614
什么...你什么意思?      当然是您决定退休之后
What... What do you mean? Oh, I mean when you decide to retire.

156
00:08:09,775 --> 00:08:11,588
我没要退休啊 我才刚上任
I'm not going to retire! I've only just got here!

157
00:08:14,008 --> 00:08:16,141
他们怎么就谈起下一任首相了?
Why are people talking about the next PM?

158
00:08:16,141 --> 00:08:19,447
我坚信这不过是宏观预测 首相
I'm sure it's just general speculation.

159
00:08:20,335 --> 00:08:24,647
他本人有意当首相吗?      就算他有...
Does he want to be Prime Minister? Well, even if he does...

160
00:08:24,815 --> 00:08:28,285
您当然也不至于怀疑他的忠诚吧
...surely you've got no reason to suspect his loyalty?

161
00:08:28,455 --> 00:08:31,845
他总没有在拉帮结派吧 有吗?
He isn't planning to build up a personal following, is he?

162
00:08:32,015 --> 00:08:34,609
没有吗?
Isn't he?

163
00:08:34,775 --> 00:08:38,927
有吗?      他成天都在做演说
Is he? Spends a hell of a lot of time making speeches.

164
00:08:39,095 --> 00:08:40,328
对 但这只是履行大臣职责 我相信他
Only as a loyal minister. I'm sure

165
00:08:40,328 --> 00:08:43,841
一定会在演讲中替您美言吧?
he pays tributes to you in them, doesn't he?

166
00:08:43,841 --> 00:08:47,490
有吗? 伯纳 把他最近6次讲话拿来
Does he? Bernard, get me his last six speeches.

167
00:08:47,655 --> 00:08:51,045
好 我正要去 首相
Er, yes, I'm just getting them, Prime Minister.

168
00:08:51,215 --> 00:08:53,934
他老在茶室里跟后座议员聊天
He chats up back benchers in the tea room.

169
00:08:54,095 --> 00:08:57,292
您吩咐大臣们多与党派和下院交流的
You told ministers to take more trouble to communicate.

170
00:08:57,455 --> 00:09:00,891
还请他们参加晚宴      他有吗?
And he has them round to dinner parties. Oh, does he?

171
00:09:01,055 --> 00:09:04,092
让人担心啊      就业大臣的讲话 首相
Worrying. The Employment Secretary's speeches.

172
00:09:04,255 --> 00:09:08,099
肯定在讲新任首相乃国家之契机
I'm sure he talked about the new PM bringing new hope to Britain,

173
00:09:08,099 --> 00:09:10,088
带来新时代的黎明
the dawn of a new age.

174
00:09:10,415 --> 00:09:11,441
就那本小册子
You know, that leaflet

175
00:09:11,441 --> 00:09:15,941
您让政党总部下发各大臣和选区的
you told Party HQ to issue to all MPs and constituencies.

176
00:09:16,735 --> 00:09:21,206
没有 一句都没有      这可奇怪了
No, not a word. Oh, now that IS odd.

177
00:09:21,375 --> 00:09:25,368
何止奇怪 简直可疑 相当可疑
It's more than odd, it's suspicious. Bloody suspicious!

178
00:09:25,535 --> 00:09:29,323
就算是 他总不会阴谋反对您吧
Even so, he surely isn't actively plotting against you.

179
00:09:29,495 --> 00:09:32,055
他不会吗?      他会吗?
Isn't he? Is he?

180
00:09:32,215 --> 00:09:36,606
我怎么知道他不会?      我相信您自有办法明察
How do I know he's not? I'm sure you can always find out.

181
00:09:37,375 --> 00:09:38,442
给我接组织秘书 伯纳
Get me the Chief Whip.

182
00:09:38,442 --> 00:09:40,531
是 首相 接组织秘书
Yes, Prime Minister. Get me the Chief Whip.

183
00:09:41,935 --> 00:09:45,723
马上      马上 您好 组织秘书
Now! Now! Oh, hello, Chief Whip.

184
00:09:45,895 --> 00:09:49,490
您在12号吗? 首相有急事要见您
Are you at No.12? The PM wants to see you urgently.

185
00:09:49,655 --> 00:09:52,249
马上      马上 谢谢
Now! Now! Thank you.

186
00:09:58,055 --> 00:10:00,250
汉弗莱爵士      什么 伯纳?
Sir Humphrey. Yes?

187
00:10:00,415 --> 00:10:03,248
我刚听到的事太可怕了      什么事?
I'm troubled by what I've learned. What?

188
00:10:03,415 --> 00:10:05,650
我觉得像个睁眼瞎
I feel I've had my eyes shut.

189
00:10:05,650 --> 00:10:09,269
我从没察觉内阁有阴谋反对首相
I never realised there was a plot against the Prime Minister.

190
00:10:09,895 --> 00:10:13,205
有吗? 真有意思
Is there? How interesting.

191
00:10:13,375 --> 00:10:17,163
可您说有的      没有 伯纳 我什么也没说
But you said there was. I said nothing, nothing at all.

192
00:10:17,335 --> 00:10:20,327
您是说...哦
You mean... Oh.

193
00:10:20,495 --> 00:10:22,963
您知道有没有阴谋吗?      不
Do you know if there is a plot? No.

194
00:10:23,135 --> 00:10:26,207
不知道还是不存在?      对
No, there isn't? Or, no, you don't know? Yes.

195
00:10:27,455 --> 00:10:30,765
汉弗莱爵士 就业大臣到底干了什么?
What exactly has the Employment Secretary done?

196
00:10:30,935 --> 00:10:33,104
眼下还没有 伯纳 我们得保持这个状态
Nothing yet, and we must keep it that way.

197
00:10:33,104 --> 00:10:35,702
可他的计划不好吗?
But isn't his plan a good one?

198
00:10:35,702 --> 00:10:37,806
对谁?      对国家
For whom? The country.

199
00:10:37,975 --> 00:10:40,443
这不是重点      为什么?
That is hardly the point. Why not?

200
00:10:40,615 --> 00:10:44,813
伯纳 你离职之后 打算去哪里?
Bernard, when you move on from here, where do you plan to go?

201
00:10:44,975 --> 00:10:48,126
我...我不知道
Well, I... er... I... I don't know.

202
00:10:48,295 --> 00:10:52,846
做副秘书长 主管国防采购如何?      天啊...
Like to be in charge of defence procurement? Oh, gosh...

203
00:10:53,015 --> 00:10:54,615
在散德兰 或者贝里克
In Sunderland or Berwick

204
00:10:54,615 --> 00:10:57,024
或者萝西毛?      这是地名吗?
or Lossiemouth? Is that a place?

205
00:10:57,024 --> 00:11:00,970
萝西毛? 你以为是什么?      狗粮牌子
Lossiemouth? What'd you think it was? A dog food.

206
00:11:03,055 --> 00:11:05,269
如果就业大臣得逞
If the Employment Secretary has his way,

207
00:11:05,269 --> 00:11:07,806
你就要吃三年萝西毛了
you may get a diet of Lossiemouth.

208
00:11:07,935 --> 00:11:09,653
明白?      明白
See? Yes.

209
00:11:09,815 --> 00:11:12,409
这怎么可能对国家有益?      绝对没有
How can it be good for the country? It can't.

210
00:11:12,575 --> 00:11:14,389
可您为什么建议找组织秘书
Why will the Chief Whip

211
00:11:14,389 --> 00:11:15,941
证实不存在的阴谋?
confirm a plot that doesn't exist?

212
00:11:15,941 --> 00:11:21,020
因为他只能绕弯子 组织秘书不能说没有阴谋
He's bound to hedge. The Chief Whip cannot state that

213
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:22,862
以防真的有
there's no plot just in case there is.

214
00:11:22,862 --> 00:11:24,796
他得给自己留后路 早安 组织秘书
He has to cover himself. Good morning.

215
00:11:24,796 --> 00:11:27,244
您能去私人办公室等吗?      好
Could you wait in the private office?

216
00:11:27,244 --> 00:11:32,455
伯纳 你进去 回头向我通报谈话内容
Bernard... now go in there and inform me of their conversation.

217
00:11:32,615 --> 00:11:35,175
我不一定能说 也许是机密
I'm not sure I can. It might be confidential.

218
00:11:35,335 --> 00:11:40,728
伯纳 这关系到国土安全 还有政府稳定
Bernard, the matter at issue is the stability of the government.

219
00:11:40,895 --> 00:11:43,807
可您只需知道您需要知道的事
You only need to know things on a need-to-know basis.

220
00:11:43,975 --> 00:11:46,808
我需要知道一切
I need to know everything!

221
00:11:47,855 --> 00:11:51,894
不然我怎能判断我需不需要知道?
How else can I judge whether or not I need to know it?

222
00:11:53,215 --> 00:11:55,265
所以您不需要知道的事
So you need to know things even

223
00:11:55,265 --> 00:11:56,508
您也需要知道?
when you don't need to know them?

224
00:11:57,375 --> 00:11:59,227
您需要知道 不是因为您需要知道
You need to know them because you need to

225
00:11:59,227 --> 00:12:01,337
而是为了知道您是否需要知道
know whether or not you need to know.

226
00:12:02,255 --> 00:12:04,209
就算您不需要知道 您也需要知道
If you don't need to know, you need to know so

227
00:12:04,209 --> 00:12:06,274
才能知道您不需要知道
you know there was no need to know.

228
00:12:07,135 --> 00:12:10,127
对      好 这就很清楚了
Yes! Good. That's very clear.

229
00:12:15,535 --> 00:12:17,730
组织秘书来了 首相
Chief Whip, Prime Minister.

230
00:12:19,135 --> 00:12:21,126
早安 首相
Morning, Prime Minister.

231
00:12:23,255 --> 00:12:27,453
最近情况怎样 组织秘书?      挺好的 怎么了?
How are things going, Chief Whip? Oh, quite well, really. Why?

232
00:12:28,495 --> 00:12:32,693
你没注意到什么?      眼下是比较艰难
You've noticed nothing? Well, it's a difficult time.

233
00:12:32,855 --> 00:12:35,847
后座议员骚动不安...
Bit of unrest on the back benches...

234
00:12:36,015 --> 00:12:40,167
您...到底想说什么?
What... did you have in mind precisely?

235
00:12:40,335 --> 00:12:42,371
阴谋 对领导权的挑战
A plot. A leadership challenge?

236
00:12:43,255 --> 00:12:46,053
啊 对...
Ah. Yes...

237
00:12:47,055 --> 00:12:51,253
说实话 我还没有确凿证据
Well, actually, I have no real evidence of anything.

238
00:12:51,415 --> 00:12:55,124
可你起了疑心?      我常年都起疑心的
But you have suspicions? Oh, I always have suspicions.

239
00:12:55,295 --> 00:12:59,925
到什么地步了?      只到很...很...
How far has it got? Oh, only a very... um... very... um...

240
00:13:00,095 --> 00:13:04,407
初期?      初期 据我了解
Early stage? Early stage. As far as one can tell.

241
00:13:05,215 --> 00:13:07,809
你不该找他谈谈吗 告诉他我察觉了?
Should you have a word with him?

242
00:13:07,975 --> 00:13:09,822
我不想让内阁失去他
I don't want to lose him from the Cabinet.

243
00:13:09,822 --> 00:13:12,097
我只想控制他
I... just want him under control.

244
00:13:13,815 --> 00:13:16,852
也许您应该亲自找他谈谈
Perhaps you should have a word with him yourself.

245
00:13:17,015 --> 00:13:21,486
不不 暂时不要 除了他还有谁?
No, no, no, no. No, not at this stage. Who else is involved?

246
00:13:21,655 --> 00:13:23,646
除了...
Apart from...

247
00:13:26,295 --> 00:13:29,446
除了达德利(就业大臣) 当然      达德利
Apart from Dudley, obviously. Dudley?

248
00:13:29,615 --> 00:13:34,405
对 当然 除了达德利 除了达德利还有...
Yes, of course, apart from Dudley. Well, apart from Dudley...

249
00:13:35,855 --> 00:13:39,111
现在说有点为时过早
Well, it's... um... It's a bit early to say.

250
00:13:39,111 --> 00:13:40,329
也许没什么事
There may be nothing in it.

251
00:13:40,329 --> 00:13:44,245
杰弗里 我可冒不起这个险      不 当然不行
I'm not taking any risks. No, absolutely not!

252
00:13:44,415 --> 00:13:47,532
我再下去问问
I'll go and make a few more enquiries.

253
00:13:47,695 --> 00:13:49,811
达德利?
Dudley?

254
00:13:49,975 --> 00:13:51,567
对
Yes.

255
00:13:52,735 --> 00:13:55,334
我猜首相支持提案
I presume the PM's in favour of the scheme

256
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:57,427
是因为它能降低失业率吧
because it'll reduce unemployment.

257
00:13:57,695 --> 00:14:00,687
它会显得首相在降低失业率
It'll look as if he's reducing unemployment.

258
00:14:00,855 --> 00:14:03,574
或者显得他在设法降低
Or look as if he's TRYING to reduce it.

259
00:14:03,735 --> 00:14:05,643
尽管他只是设法显得
Whereas he's only trying to look as if

260
00:14:05,643 --> 00:14:07,951
他在设法降低失业率
he's trying to reduce unemployment.

261
00:14:08,775 --> 00:14:11,812
对 因为他担心显示不出他在
Because he's worried that it doesn't LOOK as if

262
00:14:11,812 --> 00:14:14,265
设法显得设法降低失业率
he's trying to look as if he's trying to reduce it.

263
00:14:15,535 --> 00:14:16,501
你打算怎么阻止?
So how are you going to stop it?

264
00:14:19,495 --> 00:14:21,690
首相开始怀疑
The PM has come to suspect

265
00:14:21,855 --> 00:14:24,534
这计划也许是就业大臣
the plan may be the start of a leadership bid

266
00:14:24,534 --> 00:14:26,531
夺取领导权的第一步
by the Employment Secretary.

267
00:14:26,531 --> 00:14:29,528
真荒唐 可职位越高
How ridiculous, but the higher the office,

268
00:14:29,528 --> 00:14:31,380
妄想症也越重
the higher the level of paranoia.

269
00:14:31,895 --> 00:14:35,604
幸好 是这样的 可妄想症需要动力
Fortunately, yes, but paranoia needs something to feed on.

270
00:14:35,775 --> 00:14:38,767
没有比媒体泄密更好的动力了
Nothing like press leaks for paranoia fodder.

271
00:14:38,935 --> 00:14:40,906
这个标题怎样
What if there should be a headline about

272
00:14:44,415 --> 00:14:46,610
"惨遭首相封杀"?
being blocked by the Prime Minister?

273
00:14:46,775 --> 00:14:50,609
有人失足落水了      幸运的话
Man overboard! With any luck.

274
00:14:50,775 --> 00:14:55,053
可问题是 内阁秘书不能参与泄密
But the trouble is a Cabinet Secretary cannot be party to a leak.

275
00:14:55,215 --> 00:14:59,686
不 当然不能      然而前任内阁秘书...
No, of course not. Whereas a FORMER Cabinet Secretary...

276
00:15:02,135 --> 00:15:06,447
可想而知 作为信息自由运动主席
Presumably, as chairman of the Campaign for Freedom of Information

277
00:15:06,615 --> 00:15:11,370
你有责任把某些事实公布出去吧
you have a... a duty to make certain facts available.

278
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:15,448
你是暗示我把机密信息透给媒体吗?
Are you suggesting I give confidential information to the press?

279
00:15:15,615 --> 00:15:17,765
当然不是 阿诺德
Certainly not, Arnold.

280
00:15:17,935 --> 00:15:20,927
这是机密假信息
This is confidential disinformation.

281
00:15:21,095 --> 00:15:23,211
啊 那就不同了
Ah, that's different.

282
00:15:27,295 --> 00:15:32,892
抱歉 这是给首相的晚报吗? 能看看吗? 多谢
Oh, excuse me. Is that the evening paper for the Prime Minister? May I?

283
00:15:35,015 --> 00:15:39,486
很好 听着 我有急事找他谈
Ah, good. Look, I have to have an urgent word with him.

284
00:15:39,655 --> 00:15:41,163
不知你能不能稍后送进去
I wonder if you'd be kind enough to bring that in in,

285
00:15:41,163 --> 00:15:45,897
过3分钟吧 谢谢
say, three minutes. Thank you.

286
00:15:48,335 --> 00:15:52,533
谢谢 伯纳      汉弗莱 我知道怎么回事了
Thank you, Bernard. Humphrey, I know what's been going on!

287
00:15:52,695 --> 00:15:54,413
您知道了?      对 我知道了
You do? Yes!

288
00:15:54,575 --> 00:15:56,658
有人背着我暗中勾结
A scheme has been hatched behind my back,

289
00:15:56,658 --> 00:16:00,431
一场背信弃义的阴谋 我绝不会轻饶
a disloyal, treacherous plot, and I won't tolerate it.

290
00:16:00,935 --> 00:16:03,244
我跟组织秘书谈过了      怎样?
I've spoken to the Chief Whip. And?

291
00:16:03,415 --> 00:16:08,205
他说没证据 但他也怀疑 他要去查问
He says he has his suspicions. He's going to make enquiries.

292
00:16:08,375 --> 00:16:11,685
等有了确凿证据再向我汇报 你看
He can't tell me more till he has something solid. You see?

293
00:16:11,855 --> 00:16:15,245
什么?      就业大臣在搞阴谋
What? The Employment Secretary is plotting!

294
00:16:15,415 --> 00:16:20,125
还不懂 汉弗莱?      我只能说 我太惊讶了
Come on, Humphrey! Well, I must say, I am surprised.

295
00:16:21,575 --> 00:16:24,772
我总以为您的内阁大臣都很忠诚呢
I should've thought all your Cabinet were loyal.

296
00:16:24,935 --> 00:16:28,530
忠诚 你知道内阁大臣的忠诚是什么
Loyal! You know what loyalty in a Cabinet minister means?

297
00:16:28,695 --> 00:16:29,985
他对自己下台的恐惧
His fear of losing his own job is

298
00:16:29,985 --> 00:16:32,941
稍稍压过想取代我的愿望
slightly greater than his hope of pinching mine.

299
00:16:33,495 --> 00:16:35,884
对 但你们有集体负责制...
But with collective responsibility...

300
00:16:36,055 --> 00:16:38,019
集体负责 就是政府一出成绩
If we do something popular,

301
00:16:38,019 --> 00:16:39,499
他们都放风说是他们的主意
they leak that it was their idea.

302
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:43,052
要是失败了 就放风说他们本来就反对
If it's unpopular, they leak they were against it.

303
00:16:43,215 --> 00:16:46,924
我们政府的原则是集体不负责制
We're governed on the principle of collective irresponsibility.

304
00:16:47,095 --> 00:16:49,655
他们为什么想取代您?
Why do they want your job?

305
00:16:49,815 --> 00:16:51,771
因为政府里就我一个人
Because I'm the only member of the government

306
00:16:51,771 --> 00:16:55,708
不可能下周被踢到北爱尔兰去
who can't be sent to Northern Ireland next week.

307
00:16:56,055 --> 00:17:01,254
我不能相信就业大臣真的在阴谋反对您
I can't believe that the Employment Secretary is plotting against you.

308
00:17:01,415 --> 00:17:03,610
你还要什么证据?
What more proof do you want?

309
00:17:03,775 --> 00:17:07,566
首相 把国防机构搬到北方的提案
This proposal to send defence establishments up north

310
00:17:07,566 --> 00:17:09,514
肯定会泄漏给媒体吧?
is bound to be leaked to the press.

311
00:17:09,514 --> 00:17:13,245
肯定会      如果媒体说是他的计划
Bound to be. If it were leaked as HIS plan,

312
00:17:13,415 --> 00:17:17,727
您的怀疑就证实了 但我相信计划会被归给政府
it'd confirm your suspicions, but I'm sure it'll go out as a government plan.

313
00:17:17,895 --> 00:17:21,604
你相信? 我可不信      啊 晚报来了
Are you? I'm not. Ah, the evening paper.

314
00:17:25,135 --> 00:17:30,892
老天啊 看 流氓 你要的证据 汉弗莱
Good God! Look! Swine! There's your proof, Humphrey!

315
00:17:32,255 --> 00:17:34,849
天哪 我太震惊了
Good heavens, I'm astonished.

316
00:17:36,935 --> 00:17:40,405
"白厅知情人士透露 这份创意计划"
"Sources in Whitehall report that this imaginative plan,

317
00:17:40,575 --> 00:17:43,726
"由就业大臣一手提出"
"an initiative by the Employment Secretary,

318
00:17:43,895 --> 00:17:46,887
"却惨遭首相封杀"
"has been blocked by the Prime Minister"?!

319
00:17:47,055 --> 00:17:49,250
他怎么敢这样
How dare he!

320
00:17:49,415 --> 00:17:51,565
他怎么敢? 我...我...
How dare he! I'm... I'm...

321
00:17:51,735 --> 00:17:54,203
无话可说?      无话可说
Speechless? Speechless!

322
00:17:55,255 --> 00:17:57,102
我一路为他保驾
I've backed him all along!

323
00:17:57,102 --> 00:17:59,003
我为他的破提案力排众议
I've fought for his sodding plan!

324
00:17:59,003 --> 00:18:00,680
他第一个内阁职位就是我给的
I gave him his first Cabinet post,

325
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,591
我待他像亲生儿子
treated him like a son!

326
00:18:02,775 --> 00:18:04,845
这就是我得到的报答
This is the thanks I get!

327
00:18:05,015 --> 00:18:09,850
内阁同僚之负义 何猛于毒蛇之尖牙啊
How sharper than a serpent's tooth it is to have a thankless Cabinet colleague.

328
00:18:10,015 --> 00:18:12,927
是嫉妒 达德利满心嫉妒
It's envy. Dudley is consumed with envy.

329
00:18:13,095 --> 00:18:14,253
这是七宗达德利罪(死罪)之一
It's one of the seven Dudley sins.

330
00:18:14,253 --> 00:18:16,061
谢谢 伯纳
Thank you Bernard

331
00:18:20,535 --> 00:18:26,371
首相 要不要起草接受他辞呈的信?
Prime Minister, shall we start to draft your letter accepting his resignation?

332
00:18:26,535 --> 00:18:28,956
没那么简单 他不会承认泄密
It's not that simple. He'll deny he leaked,

333
00:18:28,956 --> 00:18:30,598
我以什么理由炒他?
so why am I sacking him?

334
00:18:30,598 --> 00:18:33,457
再说 他变成后座议员更危险
He'll be more dangerous on the back benches.

335
00:18:33,457 --> 00:18:36,544
炒了他 他都不用假装忠诚了
Sacked, he doesn't have to pretend to be loyal.

336
00:18:36,544 --> 00:18:42,211
那您要顺着他的计划来?      不行 现在不行
So you mean you'll go ahead with his plan? I can't. Not now.

337
00:18:42,375 --> 00:18:44,745
会显得像他击败了我 这个险不能冒
It'll look as though he's defeated me. I can't risk that.

338
00:18:44,745 --> 00:18:47,215
计划确实不错
It's a good plan.

339
00:18:47,735 --> 00:18:51,569
那么 也许...不不 我...
So... perha... Er... no, no, I...

340
00:18:51,735 --> 00:18:55,284
首相 您不会不知如何是好了吧?
Prime Minister, you're not being indecisive, are you?

341
00:18:55,455 --> 00:18:58,447
不 不
No, no!

342
00:18:58,615 --> 00:19:03,609
不 我只是下不了决心      好吧 也许我能帮忙
No, I just can't make up my mind. Well, perhaps I can help.

343
00:19:03,775 --> 00:19:06,972
怎么?      理论上 我不该给您看这个
How? Technically, I shouldn't be showing you this.

344
00:19:07,135 --> 00:19:10,491
怎么? 我不是首相吗      毫无疑问
Why not? I'm Prime Minister, aren't I? Indeed you are!

345
00:19:11,455 --> 00:19:14,174
所以我才不该给您看
That's why I shouldn't show it to you.

346
00:19:14,335 --> 00:19:19,807
是国防部内部文件草案 国防大臣都没看过
It's a Ministry of Defence internal paper. The Secretary hasn't seen it yet.

347
00:19:19,975 --> 00:19:22,760
但您看 其中对就业大臣的计划
But it casts grave doubts

348
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,813
提出了严重质疑      是吗?
on the plan. Does it?

349
00:19:24,813 --> 00:19:27,055
里面指出 他提到的许多贵重建筑
Many of the valuable buildings

350
00:19:27,055 --> 00:19:29,019
根本不能卖
he quotes can't be sold.

351
00:19:29,295 --> 00:19:34,289
有些是古迹 有些受规划控制 搬迁成本太过高昂
Some are listed, some have planning controls. The cost would be prohibitive.

352
00:19:34,455 --> 00:19:38,164
还会在伦敦周边和东英格兰造成严重失业
It'd create unemployment in the Home Counties and East Anglia

353
00:19:38,335 --> 00:19:44,729
第3部分 一页页都是基于战略考量的反对意见
and in Part 3 there are objections on the grounds of military strategy.

354
00:19:44,895 --> 00:19:49,491
这些都真实可靠吗?      都是国防部的手笔
And all this is honest and accurate? It comes from the Ministry of Defence.

355
00:19:52,495 --> 00:19:55,487
即便如此 也有可能真实可靠吧
Even so, it COULD be honest and accurate.

356
00:19:56,495 --> 00:20:00,693
告诉你 我觉得公众有权知道这些
You know, I think the public has a right to know this.

357
00:20:01,495 --> 00:20:03,690
这是顶级机密文件
It is a top-secret document.

358
00:20:06,695 --> 00:20:11,291
话说回来 军官们是出了名的口没遮拦
On the other hand, the service chiefs are notorious for their indiscretion.

359
00:20:11,455 --> 00:20:15,334
有可能流到某个不负责任的记者手中
It could find its way into the hands of some irresponsible journalist.

360
00:20:15,495 --> 00:20:20,205
对 或者某几个...      某几个 是的 首相
Quite. Or several irresponsible... Several, indeed, Prime Minister.

361
00:20:20,375 --> 00:20:23,970
当然 我绝不能参与      当然不能
Of course, I could never be a party to that. Certainly not.

362
00:20:24,135 --> 00:20:25,482
那么 首相 我们是不是要
So, shall we defer further discussion

363
00:20:25,482 --> 00:20:28,157
把就业大臣计划的讨论
of the Employment Secretary's plan

364
00:20:28,157 --> 00:20:30,886
无限制延期?
to an unspecified future date?

365
00:20:31,495 --> 00:20:33,884
好 不管它了
Yeah, let's drop it.

366
00:20:34,055 --> 00:20:37,730
首相 我先疏浚管道去了
Prime Minister. Meanwhile, I'll go and attend to the plumbing.

367
00:20:40,295 --> 00:20:45,415
他什么时候会泄密?      我要他泄密了吗 伯纳?
When's he going to leak it? Did I ask for a leak, Bernard?

368
00:20:46,495 --> 00:20:50,693
倒没有明说...不 您没有      对 我没有
Well, not in so many... No, you didn't. No, I didn't.

369
00:20:50,855 --> 00:20:54,768
我偶尔开些内部新闻发布会 可我从不泄密
I occasionally have confidential press briefings, but I have never leaked.

370
00:20:54,935 --> 00:20:56,607
又是不规则动词 对吧?
Another irregular verb

371
00:20:56,607 --> 00:20:59,238
某甲开内部新闻发布会 某乙泄密
I give confidential press briefings, you leak,

372
00:20:59,238 --> 00:21:04,085
某丙被控违反官方保密法2A条款
he's been charged under Section 2A of the Official Secrets Act.

373
00:21:09,095 --> 00:21:12,007
早安 首相      早安
Good morning, Prime Minister. Morning.

374
00:21:15,015 --> 00:21:18,325
早安 首相      你们看报纸了吗?
Good morning. Have you seen the papers?

375
00:21:18,495 --> 00:21:20,843
看了      达德利回应了泄密的事
Indeed. Dudley's replied to the press about that leak.

376
00:21:20,843 --> 00:21:23,551
他说他没泄密 有人害他的
he said he leaked nothing

377
00:21:23,551 --> 00:21:25,574
他要求公开调查
He's demanded a public inquiry.

378
00:21:25,735 --> 00:21:30,570
真惊人      调查从来查不出泄密人
Shocking. Inquiries never find the true source of a leak.

379
00:21:31,495 --> 00:21:36,091
但我们知道是谁 您要我们...      伯纳
But we know the true source. You asked us... Bernard.

380
00:21:37,975 --> 00:21:39,218
你该不是暗示
You're not suggesting

381
00:21:39,218 --> 00:21:41,098
泄密是我指使的吧
I authorised this leak?

382
00:21:41,098 --> 00:21:45,486
不 我...没错...就是说...我想起来了 抱歉
Er, no, I... er... That is, yes. Um, I mean... Oh, I remember now. Sorry.

383
00:21:47,335 --> 00:21:51,328
你想起什么了 伯纳?      您说什么就是什么
What do you remember, Bernard? Whatever you want.

384
00:21:51,495 --> 00:21:54,293
我要公众相信根本没有分歧
I want the public to know there are no divisions.

385
00:21:54,455 --> 00:21:57,811
可确实有啊      我不想它们加倍
But there are. I don't want them multiplied.

386
00:21:57,975 --> 00:22:01,411
首相 如果把分开的加倍 就回到原点了
If you multiply divisions, you get back to where you started.

387
00:22:02,775 --> 00:22:06,927
把4分成2份 得2 再加倍 还是4
If you divide four by two, you get two. If you multiply it, you get four.

388
00:22:07,095 --> 00:22:09,814
除非您的倍数和分数不同...
Unless you multiply different divisions...

389
00:22:09,975 --> 00:22:13,934
4分2份...伯纳 请他们进来      是 首相
Four by two... Bernard, send them in. Yes, Prime Minister.

390
00:22:15,015 --> 00:22:17,799
汉弗莱 我想把就业大臣留在内阁
I want to keep the Employment Secretary in the Cabinet,

391
00:22:17,799 --> 00:22:19,558
国防大臣也是
and the Defence Secretary,

392
00:22:19,775 --> 00:22:22,608
但我不能再放任不管了
but I can't let this row go on any longer.

393
00:22:22,775 --> 00:22:27,166
我不能显得被就业大臣打败 风险太大了
I can't allow the Employment Secretary to be seen to defeat me.

394
00:22:27,335 --> 00:22:31,328
那我建议您 提请委员会同意这三点
I suggest you ask the Committee to agree to these three points.

395
00:22:31,495 --> 00:22:34,089
第一 内阁决议必须接受
First, they accept Cabinet's decision.

396
00:22:34,255 --> 00:22:37,964
第二 要有个冷却期 讨论中止
Secondly, there's a cooling-off period with no further discussion.

397
00:22:38,135 --> 00:22:41,494
最后 未来所有讲话和媒体声明
Further, that all speeches and press statements

398
00:22:41,494 --> 00:22:43,206
要由内阁办公室审查
are cleared with the Cabinet Office.

399
00:22:44,015 --> 00:22:49,135
很好 这就没问题了 对 第一点 冷却期
Splendid. That should do it, yes. Point one, a cooling-off period.

400
00:22:49,295 --> 00:22:52,605
第二点 讨论中止...
Point two, no more decisions or discussions...

401
00:22:52,775 --> 00:22:55,209
不对 第二是什么来着?
No, what was the second one?

402
00:22:55,375 --> 00:22:58,970
我记不住...      我写给您 首相
I can't quite... I'll write it down for you, Prime Minister.

403
00:23:00,015 --> 00:23:02,734
先生们 请坐
Ah, gentlemen, please be seated.

404
00:23:03,855 --> 00:23:07,006
你们都拿到议程副本了
You've all had a copy of the agenda.

405
00:23:07,175 --> 00:23:11,134
第一项 上次会议纪要
Item one, minutes of the last meeting.

406
00:23:11,295 --> 00:23:13,684
首相 抱歉 有个程序问题
Excuse me, a point of order.

407
00:23:13,855 --> 00:23:18,133
我的国防机构重组计划不在议程上
My plan for defence establishment relocation is not on the agenda.

408
00:23:18,295 --> 00:23:20,490
正是 达德利      为什么?
That is correct, Dudley. Why not?

409
00:23:20,655 --> 00:23:24,449
因为泄密 媒体已经在口诛笔伐
This leaking is creating a damaging press row.

410
00:23:24,449 --> 00:23:26,306
我不能让内阁显得有分歧
I can't allow the Cabinet to seem divided.

411
00:23:26,306 --> 00:23:30,005
是有分歧      所以尤其不能显出来
It is divided. That's why it mustn't look it.

412
00:23:30,175 --> 00:23:35,488
事情很复杂 所以我决定延期讨论
It's a very complex issue and I've decided to defer further discussion.

413
00:23:35,655 --> 00:23:39,045
我不明白 您上次还支持的      不 我没有
You were in favour of it last time. No, I wasn't.

414
00:23:39,215 --> 00:23:44,050
您有 大家都支持 除了国防部      不 大家没有
You were! So was everyone, except Defence. No, they weren't.

415
00:23:44,215 --> 00:23:46,198
他们有 您承诺深入讨论的
They were! You promised further discussion!

416
00:23:46,198 --> 00:23:50,139
抱歉打扰一下  我不能苟同
Um... I'm sorry to interrupt, but I think not.

417
00:23:50,139 --> 00:23:53,127
什么?      没有过这种承诺
What? There was no such promise.

418
00:23:53,295 --> 00:23:58,494
首相也从未支持提案 否则 会议纪要上会有记载
And the PM did not support. If he had, it would appear in the minutes.

419
00:23:58,655 --> 00:24:01,453
上面没有      没有吗?
It doesn't. Doesn't it?

420
00:24:01,615 --> 00:24:04,697
首相 为什么我要求的深入讨论
Prime Minister, why was my request for a

421
00:24:04,697 --> 00:24:06,873
和您的回答没有记载?
further discussion not minuted?

422
00:24:06,873 --> 00:24:09,453
我...      首相
I... Er, Prime Minister.

423
00:24:10,695 --> 00:24:14,167
委员会讨论或决议的共性是
It is characteristic of committee decisions that

424
00:24:14,167 --> 00:24:16,802
每个与会人员都对它记忆犹新
every member has a vivid recollection of them

425
00:24:16,855 --> 00:24:21,053
而每人的记忆又和别人大相径庭
and that every member's recollection differs from every other member's.

426
00:24:21,215 --> 00:24:25,811
因此按惯例 所谓官方决议 是且只是
Consequently, we accept the convention that official decisions are those

427
00:24:25,975 --> 00:24:28,364
官方人员记入纪要的决议
recorded in the minutes by the officials.

428
00:24:28,535 --> 00:24:31,732
因此顺理成章 不可避免地
From which it emerges, with an elegant inevitability,

429
00:24:31,895 --> 00:24:33,373
任何官方达成的决议
that any officially reached decision

430
00:24:33,373 --> 00:24:36,199
都会被官方记入纪要
will have been recorded by the officials.

431
00:24:36,455 --> 00:24:38,641
而官方纪要里没有的
Any decision not recorded

432
00:24:38,641 --> 00:24:39,788
就从未被官方达成过
has not been officially reached,

433
00:24:39,788 --> 00:24:42,727
哪怕个别成员自以为记得有过
even if one or more members believe they can recollect it,

434
00:24:42,895 --> 00:24:46,205
因此 就这件事来说 如果官方确实达成了决议
so, in this case, if the decision had been officially reached,

435
00:24:46,375 --> 00:24:48,218
它一定会在官方纪要里
it would've been recorded by the officials,

436
00:24:48,218 --> 00:24:50,926
但它没记录 因此不存在
and it isn't, so it wasn't.

437
00:24:54,495 --> 00:24:56,486
我说吧
Told you so.

438
00:24:56,655 --> 00:24:59,044
这是篡改 首相...
This is a fiddle! Prime Minister...

439
00:24:59,215 --> 00:25:01,365
别说了 这必须停止      是的 必须停下来
No, this must stop. Yes, it must!

440
00:25:01,535 --> 00:25:05,733
我拟了三点计划 我们都必须遵守
I have drawn up a three-point plan to which we must all adhere.

441
00:25:05,895 --> 00:25:09,285
第一...第一是什么来着?
Point one... What was point one?

442
00:25:10,295 --> 00:25:15,244
谢谢 第一 每人都必须接受集体决议 达德利
Oh, thank you. Point one, everyone will accept collective decisions, Dudley.

443
00:25:15,415 --> 00:25:19,613
我很乐意 哪些是集体决议?      我说了算
I am perfectly willing to. How are they defined? I define them.

444
00:25:21,375 --> 00:25:25,846
第二 国防重组事宜进入冷却期
Point two, there will be a cooling-off period on defence relocations.

445
00:25:26,015 --> 00:25:31,487
第三...看不清 申什么?      不 审查所有讲话...
Point three... Can't read this. Cleaning what? No, CLEARING all speeches...

446
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:33,475
哦 对 所有讲话和媒体声明
All speeches and press statements

447
00:25:33,475 --> 00:25:35,529
要由内阁办公室清查
must be cleared with the Cabinet Office.

448
00:25:35,529 --> 00:25:38,827
我不能接受第二点 根本没讨论过
We can't cool off discussion on

449
00:25:38,827 --> 00:25:40,621
冷却讨论从何谈起?
something that hasn't been discussed yet

450
00:25:40,975 --> 00:25:45,253
我也绝不接受我的言论都得由他审查
and I cannot accept that anything I say must be cleared by HIM.

451
00:25:45,415 --> 00:25:47,485
他不能查禁我想说的话
He won't clear what I want to say.

452
00:25:47,655 --> 00:25:51,489
这是我的决定 你必须接受      我不接受
That is my decision and you must accept it. I won't accept it!

453
00:25:56,375 --> 00:26:00,084
达德利 恐怕你得考虑自己的位置了
Well, Dudley, I'm afraid you must consider your position.

454
00:26:05,055 --> 00:26:06,374
首相      什么?
Prime Minister. Yes?

455
00:26:06,535 --> 00:26:10,767
我有些消息 您要先听坏消息吗?
I have news. Do you want the bad news first?

456
00:26:10,935 --> 00:26:15,247
还有坏的和好的啊      不 坏的和更坏的
There's bad news and good news? No, bad news and worse news.

457
00:26:15,415 --> 00:26:18,612
就业大臣辞职了 这是辞呈
The Employment Secretary has resigned. His letter.

458
00:26:18,775 --> 00:26:22,484
我真不想失去他的      您要听更坏的吗?
I didn't want to lose him. Would you like the worse news now?

459
00:26:22,655 --> 00:26:27,410
他指控您专制独裁 大兴总统制政府
He's accused you of being dictatorial.

460
00:26:28,295 --> 00:26:30,684
好吧 这我倒不介意
Oh. Well, I don't mind that.

461
00:26:31,775 --> 00:26:35,673
其实也不错吧? 人民喜欢铁腕领导人
Rather good, isn't it? People like to know they've got a strong leader.

462
00:26:35,673 --> 00:26:39,172
独裁是吗?      对 铁腕领导人会很新奇的
Dictatorial, eh? It will be a new pleasure for them.

463
00:26:39,335 --> 00:26:41,724
不 不会的      不 不会的
No, it won't. No, it won't.

464
00:26:41,895 --> 00:26:44,362
汉弗莱 我真为他的辞职难过
Humphrey, I'm upset about this resignation.

465
00:26:44,362 --> 00:26:46,414
是你的三点计划激发的
YOUR three-point plan provoked it.

466
00:26:46,414 --> 00:26:49,288
没错 首相 可据我了解
Yes, indeed, Prime Minister, but I understand

467
00:26:49,455 --> 00:26:53,653
就业大臣无论如何都打算辞职了
the Employment Secretary was planning to resign soon in any case.

468
00:26:53,815 --> 00:26:56,010
是吗? 为什么 什么时候?
Was he? Why? And when?

469
00:26:56,175 --> 00:26:58,567
财政预算发表日 理由是
On budget day, as it was expected to give him

470
00:26:58,567 --> 00:27:02,025
拨给他的失业应对资金不够
insufficient money to deal with unemployment.

471
00:27:02,025 --> 00:27:05,087
天 那就丢人了      但会让他名声大噪的
Damaging. It would've made him extremely popular.

472
00:27:05,255 --> 00:27:06,521
也许还是我赶走他好
Perhaps it's as well I made him go.

473
00:27:06,521 --> 00:27:10,114
首相 您处理得简直绝妙
Prime Minister, you handled it brilliantly!

474
00:27:10,615 --> 00:27:12,379
您逼他为一件晦涩的
You forced him to resign on an obscure

475
00:27:12,379 --> 00:27:15,397
行政问题辞职 您占主动
administrative issue of your choosing,

476
00:27:15,432 --> 00:27:18,367
而不是他自行选定的政策问题
rather than on a policy issue of his choosing.

477
00:27:18,535 --> 00:27:23,290
没人会支持他 因为没人明白怎么回事 神来之笔
Nobody will support him because nobody will understand why he's gone

478
00:27:23,455 --> 00:27:26,253
对 是挺绝的 对吧?
Yes... it was pretty clever, wasn't it?

479
00:27:26,415 --> 00:27:28,451
无懈可击 首相
Oh, masterly!

480
00:27:28,615 --> 00:27:31,607
这份媒体声明 您可以考虑发布
Here's a press statement you might release.

481
00:27:31,775 --> 00:27:35,973
要我打给比尔吗?      不 伯纳 我来找比尔
Shall I phone Bill? No, Bernard, I shall phone Bill.

482
00:27:36,135 --> 00:27:38,126
专制独裁 是吗?
Dictatorial, hm?

483
00:27:39,935 --> 00:27:43,723
我倒不知道他打算为预算案辞职呢
I didn't know he was thinking of resigning over the budget.

484
00:27:43,895 --> 00:27:47,490
我也不知道      您说这不是真的?
Nor did I. You mean it's not true?

485
00:27:47,655 --> 00:27:52,046
我没说是真的 我说据我理解是真的
I didn't say it was true. I said I understood it to be true.

486
00:27:52,215 --> 00:27:56,003
也许我误会了      您也不知是真是假?
I may have misunderstood. So you don't know it's true?

487
00:27:56,175 --> 00:27:57,878
我不能说是假的 可能是真的
I don't know it's not. It might be.

488
00:27:57,878 --> 00:27:59,697
一切都可能是真的
Anything might be!

489
00:27:59,697 --> 00:28:03,205
正是 有进步 伯纳
Exactly. Well done, Bernard.

490
00:28:03,375 --> 00:28:05,366
记下来 比尔
Take this down, Bill.

491
00:28:05,535 --> 00:28:07,925
"我心存疑虑 我们审查了他的计划"
"I'm puzzled because his plan was being studied,

492
00:28:07,925 --> 00:28:11,682
"发现成本可能远高于预期"
but there was a danger of much greater cost

493
00:28:11,895 --> 00:28:16,491
"却不能必然达成促进就业的目标"
"without necessarily achieving the employment objectives."

494
00:28:16,655 --> 00:28:19,647
好 印好了送来给我
Fine. Send it up to me when it's typed.

495
00:28:20,495 --> 00:28:23,805
汉弗莱 看来这次又多亏你了
Well, Humphrey, looks as if you've done me a good turn.

496
00:28:23,975 --> 00:28:27,570
的确 首相      不过真可惜
Yes, indeed, Prime Minister. Pity, though.

497
00:28:27,735 --> 00:28:31,774
是啊 可他确实阴谋反对您 您自己说的
Yes. But he was plotting against you, you said so yourself.

498
00:28:31,935 --> 00:28:34,813
对 等等 我有主意了
Yes. Hold on, I've got an idea!

499
00:28:34,975 --> 00:28:36,772
首相
Prime Minister!

500
00:28:38,015 --> 00:28:42,327
既然就业大臣走了 我们可以重启计划了
Now that the Employment Secretary's gone, we could reinstate the plan!

501
00:28:43,375 --> 00:28:45,172
可是...
But...

502
00:28:45,335 --> 00:28:48,003
明白了吧 我现在可以放手去干
I could press on with it now and

503
00:28:48,003 --> 00:28:49,842
不会显得软弱 而会显得强悍
it won't look like weakness, but strength!

504
00:28:49,842 --> 00:28:53,087
可整个目的就是...      是什么?
But the whole point was... Was what?

505
00:28:53,255 --> 00:28:57,726
该不是为了阻止计划吧?      不不
It wasn't to stop the plan, surely? No, no, no, no, no.

506
00:28:57,895 --> 00:29:01,365
是为了...呃...
It was to... um... um... er... er...

507
00:29:01,535 --> 00:29:04,925
树立您的威信      正是 我已经完成了
...establish your authority. Exactly. And I've done that.

508
00:29:05,095 --> 00:29:08,292
所以 如果重启提案 就能表明我并没反对
So, if we recreate the plan, it'll show I wasn't against it

509
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:12,448
达德利的辞职就没意义了 对吧?
and that Dudley's resignation was pointless, right?

510
00:29:12,615 --> 00:29:17,006
就列为下次会议第一项议程 好吗?
Put it top of the agenda for the next Cabinet... OK?

511
00:29:18,655 --> 00:29:21,044
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

512
00:29:21,859 --> 00:29:26,045
(注: 本集暗讽1985-85年
英国Westland直升机事件)

513
00:29:27,372 --> 00:29:37,570
